    <GaugingStation location="Ness-side" name="Ness" number="6007">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station; flow regime affected by Loch Ness and other storage within the catchment.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Fully calibrated to maximum recorded flow. Frequent recalibration of low flow rating due to alteration of stop-log configuration on weir which forms control. Ratings vary in mid-sections, the one shown is the common upper limb.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Velocity area station 80m wide. Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2025 (WINFAP Files v14).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">1975, 1976, 1977 notably dry summers.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Hydrograph damped by influence of Loch Ness. Caledonian Canal lockages bypass station but, overall, small net impact. Hydro-electric power schemes on Garry, Moriston and Foyers tributaries utilise runoff from 56% of catchment, can cause abrupt changes in flow e.g. July 2000.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Large SW/NE trending Highland catchment. Predominantly impermeable bedrock, less than half with superficial deposits. Mountainous with significant afforestation and grasslands.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">H</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Gauged and calibrated to 3.324m, with a measured flow of 795 cumecs." suitable="Yes" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
